diff --git a/docs/PLUGINS.md b/docs/PLUGINS.md
index 2aaf62b..57922a1 100644
--- a/docs/PLUGINS.md
+++ b/docs/PLUGINS.md
@@ -433,3 +433,16 @@ node sekaipop/tests/plugin-test/form_unit.js          # what Settings shows: the
 sh sekaipop/tests/plugin-test/plugin_state_test.sh     # the state script, against a throwaway folder
 node sekaipop/tests/preset-widgets-test/registry_unit.js
 ```
+
+
+## Proposed native extension surfaces (additive API 1)
+
+`extensions: ["dock", "wallpaper", "settings"]` declares optional surfaces, implemented by fixed entry files `Dock.qml`, `Wallpaper.qml`, `Settings.qml`. The manager only clones/links the repository. No install hooks run. One dock/wallpaper provider is selected deterministically by plugin id; conflicting providers must not be installed together in this initial proposal.
+
+The service host advertises `capabilities`: `native-dock-v1`, `native-wallpaper-v1`, `native-settings-v1`, `transient-palette-v1`. Services may implement `extensionEnabled(slot)` to switch off a surface without changing shell files.
+
+Dock host: base widget settings/service/theme plus the live dock item, geometry, media source, lyrics, hover/edit/desktop-empty state and monitor palette. Dock entry outputs `fits`, `ownsHousing`, `widthExtra`, `heightExtra`, `headerHeight`, `iconsOffset`, `iconsOpacity`, `iconsScale`, `suppressMediaKey`. Wallpaper host: theme/settings/service, screenName, configured widget rectangles, barEdge/barExtent, working and setSetting. Settings host: state/theme, opened, close(), screenName, native phone capture item/rect and viewport rect. Settings entry exposes `showing` while its exit animation completes.
+
+Theme IPC exposes renewable palette leases (`musicSet`, `musicClear`, `musicStatus`) with baseline restoration and expiry. Persistent theme settings are not the music override. Existing desktop/bar plugins are unchanged.
+
+This section documents a proposal; upstream review and version assignment are required before advertising support in the reviewed catalogue.
